# Java Engineering Handbook

Reference: `content/java-engineering/top-100-java-interview-questions.md`, `content/java-engineering/hashmap-internals.md`

## Audience

Senior engineers, leads, and **architects** — interview preparation, quick revision, production decisions. **Not** a beginner tutorial.

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `data/java_engineering_modules.yaml` | 6 modules, **36 topics** |
| `data/java_engineering_order.yaml` | Flat prev/next nav |
| `scripts/build_java_engineering_handbook.py` | Sync order + prune orphans |
| `scripts/generate_java_handbook_refactor.py` | Regenerate interview pages (optional) |
| `content/java-engineering/<slug>.md` | Hand-maintained interview pages |

URL: `/java-engineering/<slug>/` — use `aliases:` in front matter for renamed slugs.

## Page Format (`interviewHandbook: true`)

1. **Question** as `##` heading
2. **Short Answer**
3. **Detailed Explanation**
4. **Internal Working** (when relevant)
5. **Production Notes**
6. **Common Mistakes**
7. **Follow-up Questions** with links

Difficulty and expected answer time live on the [Top 100 index](/java-engineering/top-100-java-interview-questions/) only — not repeated on depth pages.

Cheat sheets (`cheatSheet: true`): one-screen tables/diagrams only — link to depth pages.

## Modules

1. Language Fundamentals (incl. streams)
2. Collections (internals + selection)
3. Concurrency (JMM, CAS, threading, VT)
4. JVM (memory/GC, class loaders, JIT)
5. Platform APIs
6. Interview Cheat Sheets (Top 100 index)

## Out of Scope

Spring Boot, Hibernate, Maven, design patterns, DSA, NIO deep dive → other sections.

## Maintenance

```bash
python scripts/build_java_engineering_handbook.py   # sync order, prune orphans
python scripts/generate_java_handbook_refactor.py  # optional bulk regen of generated pages
```

Content is **hand-maintained** in markdown. Build script does not overwrite page bodies.
